### CyberGuard API requests for manual testing.
### Use with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request"
### above each request. Run the API first:  dotnet run --project src/CyberGuard.Api
### Enum values are numbers: PasswordRating 0 Weak, 1 Fair, 2 Strong;
### UrlVerdict 0 Unknown, 1 Safe, 2 Phishing; AlertStatus 0 New, 1 Read, 2 Reviewed.

@host = http://localhost:5042
@email = tester1@example.com
@password = Test@12345

### Health
GET {{host}}/api/v1/health

### Register (run once; a second run returns an error because the email exists)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Login (saves the token for the requests below)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### My profile
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Save a password check (only the result, never the password)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/password-checks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entropyBits": 61.4, "rating": 2, "matchedCommonOrWordlist": false }

### List password checks
GET {{host}}/api/v1/password-checks?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a wordlist entry
POST {{host}}/api/v1/wordlist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "word": "fluffy2020", "category": "pet" }

### List wordlist
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wordlist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Scan a URL
# @name urlScan
POST {{host}}/api/v1/url-scans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://paypa1.com/login" }

###
@urlScanId = {{urlScan.response.body.id}}

### Get that URL scan
GET {{host}}/api/v1/url-scans/{{urlScanId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark it as phishing
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/url-scans/{{urlScanId}}/verdict
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "verdict": 2 }

### Scan text for PII (the raw text is not stored)
# @name piiScan
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pii-scans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Email ali.khan@example.com, CNIC 35202-1234567-1, card 4111 1111 1111 1111, key AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE" }

###
@piiScanId = {{piiScan.response.body.id}}

### Save the URL scan as a report with a note
# @name report
POST {{host}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "urlScanId": "{{urlScanId}}", "note": "Check with the bank" }

### List reports
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Alerts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark all alerts as read
POST {{host}}/api/v1/alerts/mark-all-read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### History of everything
GET {{host}}/api/v1/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard (hygiene score)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cross-user check: no token must give 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/url-scans
